d on the project well before  ground was ever broken this is a time  lapse history from the 1100s to today  everything from the native american  settlements to the growing  industrial revolution to a metropolis  filled with skyscrapers  so the minute you get here you're  immersed in the story welcome to one  world observatory and we're here already  winds of change was at the center of the  project when they started  conceptualizing a design back in 2013  that includes the see forever  theater it's almost like you're bringing  the city to life  the idea is to engulf the guests  in the heartbeat and the rhythms of the  life of new york and panoramic views of  manhattan  well that's a wow the first time we were  in here with real guests  they were standing ovations and that  happened  quite a bit it was a remarkable feeling  to experience that  with them for the first time every  detail was considered and visitors from  all over the world take it in every  single day  what do you think you'll take away today  wow  just the breathtaking views and you know  just this whole story behind you know  new york what did you think in the  theater when they rose the screens we  were lost for words literally i looked  at her and i said why am i crying she  says me too  hedema has projects all over the globe  in the world's largest indoor theme park  in south korea  to north america's largest indoor water  park an interactive exhibit in the famed  world war ii museum in new orleans and  smaller creations like a pop-up at union  station in los angeles what's the budget  in a lot of these  projects can go up to hundreds of  millions of dollars some of these are  big projects but you know if the story's  right it excites us creatively then you  know a few thousand dollars  can  put something pretty magical together  this year marks henema's 20th  anniversary and their goal remains the  same what's the end game just keep on  telling stories  all of us as human beings understand  life 